<title>CHILE: Chile's Santa Isabel denies talks report.</title>
<headline>Chile's Santa Isabel denies talks report.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean supermarket chain Santa Isabel denied a newspaper report that it was in talks to buy more stores from troubled supermarket group Marmentini.</p>
<p>&quot;Santa Isabel...does not intend to acquire nor has it entered into any negotiations to acquire additional Marmentini stores,&quot; said the statement.</p>
<p>Two months ago Santa Isabel, Chile's largest supermarket chain, bought eight existing Marmentini stores as well as two under construction for $19.3 million.</p>
<p>-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595 x212</p>
